; The makespan bounds, re-asked as derivations (extension §2), so the
; cross-check oracle can compare two implementations of one question.
;
; POLARITY. Both properties here are `possible`, so both are encoded
; POSITIVELY: the relation holds the reachable situations satisfying the
; formula, and NON-EMPTY means the property holds. (`live`'s
; counterexample-set encoding, and the trap of getting it backwards, is
; explained in ../river/river.rules; nothing here is a `live`.)

(load "../libraries/scheduling.lib.pol")

(load "ct.rules")

; Finished, with the clock reading exactly tK. Non-empty ⟺ the property holds,
; so `done-by-4` empty and `done-by-5` non-empty is the optimum pinned from
; both sides.
(satisfies done-by-4 (and (all-done j) (is clk.at t4)))
(satisfies done-by-5 (and (all-done j) (is clk.at t5)))
